  "headline_finding": {
    "statement": "The measured evidence does NOT support a claim that abstention improves the system. On the held-out March-2 test split the frozen gate REDUCED selective FPR (0.0447 -> 0.0301) but INCREASED selective error rate (0.2254 -> 0.2386) and REDUCED selective F1 (0.7979 -> 0.7561), at a coverage cost of 18.1 points. Only the false-positive rate improved.",
    "why_validation_did_not_transfer": "The two splits have very different class balance: validation is 26.6% positive (392/1473) while the held-out March-2 test split is 65.5% positive (2040/3115). The F1 floor that the margin delta was selected under therefore held on validation and did NOT hold on test. This is a genuine generalisation failure of the GATE, reported as measured rather than repaired: revising the delta after seeing these test numbers is exactly the tuning this task forbids.",
    "what_is_still_demonstrated": "Abstention IS demonstrably targeted at uncertain, OOD and ambiguous windows: all 11 real Task-15 UNRELIABLE sequences abstain, 264 CAUTION sequences abstain, and 407 windows abstain for sitting within 0.05 of the frozen boundary. The layer withholds automated decisions on exactly the cases it was designed to withhold on, and never flips ALERT<->BENIGN on the windows it does decide.",
    "policy_unchanged_by_this_observation": true
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The validation split contains ZERO UNRELIABLE windows, so the hard UNRELIABLE -> ABSTAIN rule could not be evaluated on validation at all. It is a declared safety rule inherited from Task 15, not a measured one.",
    "The CAUTION branch rests on only 25 validation windows. Directional, not a stable effect estimate.",
    "Selective ERROR RATE is a misleading headline on this data. The model's positives cluster just above 0.69, so a wide margin band abstains on nearly every ALERT and lowers error simply by approaching 'always BENIGN'. The F1 floor in the selection rule exists to block exactly that, and the retained-negative share is reported on every row so the artefact stays visible.",
    "On the held-out test split the gate did NOT reproduce its validation behaviour: selective error ROSE and selective F1 FELL, and only FPR improved. See headline_finding. The gate was NOT revised in response, because that would be tuning on test.",
    "Abstention reduces FPR at a coverage cost; it does NOT improve recall and measurably worsens FNR. Whether that trade is desirable is an operational choice, not a result.",
    "The margin delta was selected under an F1 floor on a split whose class balance (26.6% positive) differs sharply from the test split (65.5% positive). Any margin-based gate selected on this validation split inherits that mismatch.",
    "The layer inherits the V4 checkpoint's train/eval scaler mismatch documented in docs/v4_baseline_manifest.json -> known_issues. It measures, and does not repair, that mismatch.",
    "No calibration was fitted, so no output may be described as a calibrated probability of correctness."
  ],
